  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The Latin meaning of volant is 'they fly.' The name stuck, and in June 1893, the settlement changed its name to Volant and it was incorporated as such.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volant%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first gristmill was built on Neshannock Creek in 1806, upstream from the current site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volant%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Thanks to the New Castle-Franklin railroad, Volant became a shopping district.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volant%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Volant is surrounded by Old Order Amish farms of the New Wilmington settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volant%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The growing need for petroleum spurred an oil boom north of Volant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volant%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The mill, which was the prime source of Volant's economy, closed its doors in the early 1960s, and the trains stopped running through Volant in 1975.",
